From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 07:21:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] windows.web: implement
 Windows.Web.Http.Filters.HttpBaseProtocolFilter.

Office's React Native host builds one of these before its networking module
will come up.  There was no Windows.Web.Http in the tree at all, so
RoGetActivationFactory reported "Failed to find library", C++/WinRT turned that
into hresult_class_not_registered, nothing caught it, and the process went to
terminate and abort.  Under Wine the access violation Office's crash handler
raises on purpose after that is re-dispatched forever -- over a million times
from one click -- so what the person sees is Word freezing the moment they open
the File tab or the account flyout, and the Backstage never drawing.

The filter is the settings object an HttpClient is built on: connections per
server, whether to follow redirects, which credentials to offer.  Those are
values the caller stores and reads back, and they are implemented, with the
defaults Windows documents.  SendRequestAsync and the members handing back a
cookie manager, a cache control, a certificate or a credential need the rest of
Windows.Web.Http, which is not here; they report that they are not implemented
rather than returning an empty object, because a caller given one cannot tell
it from the real thing and finds out somewhere else entirely.

The IIDs are from the published metadata and were checked against Office's own
binary: react-native-win32.dll carries IHttpBaseProtocolFilter and IHttpFilter,
and does not carry IHttpBaseProtocolFilter2/3/5 or IHttpCacheControl, which is
why those are not here either.

windows.web.dll was never registered, so add it to the inf as well; without
that the class is built but nothing can find it.  tools/httpfilterprobe
activates it, reaches all four interfaces, checks each documented default,
round-trips two settings, and confirms the unimplemented members fail rather
than answer: 0 of 22 checks failing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 975d730db1cd85be57b9a4e7aa71fda2d9b2d28f)

